+# Sprint V2.12 — Cartesian Goal-Region Planning
+
+**Status:** planned / held; documentation only
+**Experiment:** Experiment B
+**Robot:** planar 2R
+**Task:** known start state to position-only Cartesian goal region
+**Primary solver:** Dijkstra
+**Primary objective:** actuator travel
+
+## Sprint intent
+
+Implement the first representative task-space planning experiment after the
+centered \(\mathcal Q\)-space mechanism probes.
+
+The sprint changes the query semantics from:
+
+\[
+\mathbf q_s\rightarrow\mathbf q_g
+\]
+
+to:
+
+\[
+\mathbf q_s\rightarrow\mathcal R_X(\mathbf x_g).
+\]
+
+It does not change the certified-branch mechanism contract, shared
+uniform-\(\mathcal Q\) graph, span-matched gearbox control, or actuator-travel
+objective.
+
+## Why this sprint exists
+
+Experiment A was a controlled metric probe. A 2R motion planner is more commonly
+asked to navigate to a Cartesian position than to one arbitrarily preselected
+joint configuration.
+
+Experiment B lets the graph choose any valid final posture satisfying the
+position task. It therefore evaluates how the mechanism-induced actuator metric
+affects:
+
+- reachability under a fixed external task distribution;
+- selected IK posture;
+- path cost;
+- node expansions;
+- actuator, output, and Cartesian path geometry.
+
+## Entry gates
+
+Do not activate this sprint until:
+
+1. V2.10 Dijkstra evidence is closed and Experiment A semantics are documented;
+2. the planned same-bank A* campaign has either closed or explicitly recorded
+   why Experiment B may proceed independently;
+3. the shared-\(\mathcal Q\) pair invariant remains green;
+4. exact start query support from V2.6 remains reproducible;
+5. an ADR or contract amendment accepts goal predicates / goal-node sets;
+6. the Experiment B protocol is reviewed.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+This sprint does not include:
+
+- obstacles or collision checking;
+- dynamics or torque limits;
+- continuous local trajectory optimization;
+- Cartesian orientation;
+- 3R or 6R;
+- full-cycle/noninjective mechanisms;
+- adaptive graph refinement;
+- tuning the external task distribution to favor either mechanism;
+- a task-location atlas for the Experiment A diagonal observation.
+
+## Architecture decision required
+
+Before implementation, write an ADR covering:
+
+1. goal-set search API;
+2. deterministic termination semantics;
+3. goal-set result fields;
+4. start-query overlay compatibility;
+5. A* heuristic contract for goal sets;
+6. reachability and exclusion semantics.
+
+The generic search layer should accept either:
+
+```python
+goal_node_ids: Collection[int]
+```
+
+or:
+
+```python
+goal_test: Callable[[int], bool]
+```
+
+without introducing Cartesian knowledge into the search core.
+
+## Work packages
+
+### V2B-001 — Freeze Experiment A interpretation
+
+Add the retrospective Experiment A protocol and task-set project note.
+
+Acceptance:
+
+- V2.10 report states the canonical-probe estimand;
+- the centered midpoint design is explicit;
+- `medium_diagonal` is labeled unresolved;
+- no report calls the eight probes a random task population.
+
+### V2B-002 — Goal-set search contract
+
+Define generic goal-set semantics for Dijkstra and later A*.
+
+Requirements:
+
+- terminate when a valid best-known goal node is settled;
+- return the selected goal node;
+- preserve deterministic tie behavior;
+- reject an empty goal set with a typed status;
+- support single-goal queries as a backward-compatible special case.
+
+Tests:
+
+- single-goal equivalence;
+- two-goal oracle where the cheaper goal is not the closest by node index;
+- deterministic equal-cost goal selection;
+- disconnected goal-set behavior;
+- empty goal-set behavior.
+
+### V2B-003 — Cartesian task-domain contract
+
+Define the fixed external Cartesian domain:
+
+- coordinate frame;
+- analytic or sampled boundary;
+- relation to \(L_1,L_2\);
+- excluded base-near or singular regions, if any;
+- minimum start-goal separation;
+- area-uniform sampling method;
+- seed and schema version.
+
+The domain must be frozen before mechanism search.
+
+Deliverable:
+
+`docs/software/architecture/contracts/V2_CARTESIAN_TASK_DOMAIN.md`
+
+### V2B-004 — Uniform-area Cartesian sampler
+
+Implement direct or rejection-based area-uniform sampling.
+
+Record:
+
+- proposed samples;
+- accepted samples;
+- rejection reason counts;
+- deterministic seed;
+- empirical spatial-uniformity diagnostics.
+
+Tests:
+
+- fixed-seed reproducibility;
+- all accepted points lie in the declared domain;
+- radial/angular occupancy checks against the declared measure;
+- no dependence on mechanism descriptors or search outcomes.
+
+### V2B-005 — Start IK enumeration and frozen selection
+
+For each sampled start position:
+
+- enumerate feasible continuous 2R IK solutions;
+- filter by shared output bounds;
+- select one using the frozen bank policy;
+- record all candidates and selected index;
+- create or reuse the exact start query overlay.
+
+Tests:
+
+- forward residual within tolerance;
+- elbow-family balance under symmetric fixtures;
+- pair receives identical selected \(\mathbf q_s\);
+- no mechanism-cost field influences selection.
+
+### V2B-006 — Cartesian goal-region builder
+
+Build \(V_G\) from graph-node Cartesian coordinates and the frozen goal radius.
+
+Requirements:
+
+- one shared goal-set digest per mechanism pair and task;
+- pair invariants prove identical node membership;
+- record size, nearest-node residual, and connected-component relation to start;
+- distinguish empty goal set from disconnected nonempty goal set.
+
+### V2B-007 — Goal-radius calibration
+
+Evaluate candidate \(\epsilon_X\) values over several graph resolutions.
+
+Decision metrics:
+
+- empty-set rate for analytically reachable goals;
+- goal-set size distribution;
+- selected-goal Cartesian residual;
+- expansion-effect stability;
+- path-cost stability.
+
+Write a decision JSON. Production refuses a missing radius decision.
+
+### V2B-008 — Fixed external task-bank export
+
+Export an immutable Cartesian bank before production search.
+
+Bank fields include:
+
+- task ID;
+- start and goal Cartesian coordinates;
+- start IK candidates and selected candidate;
+- minimum-separation check;
+- domain and sampler versions;
+- seed;
+- digest.
+
+Do not regenerate in place.
+
+### V2B-009 — Result schema and failure taxonomy
+
+Add fields from the Experiment B protocol.
+
+Typed outcomes must include:
+
+- `start_unreachable`;
+- `goal_region_empty`;
+- `goal_region_disconnected`;
+- `paired_query_valid`;
+- `search_failed`;
+- `solved`.
+
+Unreachable tasks remain trial outcomes and are not silently dropped.
+
+### V2B-010 — Crossed statistical analysis
+
+Experiment B shares external tasks across mechanism pairs.
+
+Implement:
+
+- coverage summaries by task and mechanism;
+- conditional paired mechanism effect;
+- task and mechanism random/crossed variance estimates;
+- two-way clustered or crossed bootstrap confidence intervals;
+- sensitivity to structural reachability missingness.
+
+Task rows must not be analyzed as iid.
+
+### V2B-011 — Search and path diagnostics
+
+For representative tasks, render:
+
+- external task domain;
+- start position;
+- goal disk;
+- all goal graph nodes;
+- selected final node and posture;
+- \(\mathcal Q\)-space settled-node field;
+- actuator-cost field;
+- Cartesian path;
+- four-bar / gearbox side-by-side comparison.
+
+### V2B-012 — Pair-local workspace control
+
+After the external-domain primary pipeline is green, optionally add a
+pair-local reachable-workspace task bank.
+
+This control must:
+
+- have a separate experiment ID;
+- use the same goal-set planner;
+- report its different conditional estimand;
+- never be merged into the external-domain primary mean.
+
+### V2B-013 — Production orchestration
+
+Reuse V2.10 lessons:
+
+- generate-only bank stage;
+- hardware and memory calibration;
+- resolution and task-count decisions;
+- frozen confirmation subset;
+- shard retry and failure preservation;
+- sequential precision at the correct clustering unit.
+
+Production begins with Dijkstra. A* is a later solver cell after an admissible
+goal-set heuristic is accepted.
+
+## Primary outputs
+
+1. fixed external Cartesian task bank;
+2. goal-radius and resolution decisions;
+3. paired reachability table;
+4. conditional expansion-effect estimate;
+5. actuator/output/Cartesian path metrics;
+6. selected-goal posture distribution;
+7. crossed task/mechanism uncertainty;
+8. HTML evidence canvas;
+9. explicit comparison to Experiment A without combining estimands.
+
+## Scientific interpretation rules
+
+Allowed:
+
+> Under the frozen external Cartesian position-task distribution, the
+> transmission changed paired reachability-conditioned search effort by ...
+
+Allowed:
+
+> The mechanism changed which valid goal posture was cheapest under the
+> actuator-travel objective.
+
+Not allowed:
+
+> Four-bars reduce planning complexity in general.
+
+Not allowed:
+
+> The Experiment A medium diagonal proves a diagonal Cartesian advantage.
+
+## Exit criteria
+
+Sprint V2.12 is complete when:
+
+1. goal-set Dijkstra passes oracle tests;
+2. the fixed external Cartesian domain is normative;
+3. Cartesian sampling is uniform under the declared area measure;
+4. start IK selection is frozen and paired;
+5. four-bar and gearbox goal-node sets match exactly within every pair;
+6. goal radius and graph resolution have accepted decisions;
+7. unreachable and disconnected tasks remain visible outcomes;
+8. crossed uncertainty is implemented;
+9. a smoke run and production-ready dry run reproduce from one command;
+10. the report distinguishes Experiment A and Experiment B estimands.
+
+## Handoff
+
+After Experiment B review:
+
+1. decide whether the Experiment A task-location atlas is worth running;
+2. promote the trusted goal-region abstraction to 3R planar full-pose tasks
+   \((x,y,\theta)\);
+3. retain 6R \(SE(3)\) pose planning as the later research-program extension.
